# Ford Galaxy Mk2 seven-seat MPV, 2006-2015.
#
# The second-generation Galaxy, no longer a joint venture with Volkswagen:
# the large trapezoid lower grille, the higher shoulder and the seven-seat
# cabin with the third row folding into the floor. UK sales from 3 June 2006;
# facelifted in 2010 and replaced in the spring of 2015.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Galaxy
#
# Dimensions 4.820 x 1.885 x 1.725 m, wheelbase 2.850 m (Wikipedia infobox;
# width is probably over the body, since no mirror width is given, and the
# height varies with roof rails and wheel size).
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a near-level side elevation from the right-hand
# side, about 5-8 degrees toward the front and a soft 3-megapixel phone frame;
# it is a liveried taxi, so the decals cross the doors. Images 2-4 are UK cars.
#
# Colours: grade (a), the Ford Motor Company UK Customer Ordering Guide of
# 1 September 2014: Blazer Blue, Frozen White, Panther Black and Moondust
# Silver. Weights 14, 12, 10, 9, total 45, provisional.
#
# Speed 195 km/h. Comfort 80/450, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 80. Classes 1,2.
# Dates: intro June 2006, the UK launch date, to 2015 when the Mk3 replaced it.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/ford-galaxy-mk2.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/ford-galaxy-mk2.dae. References:
# citycars/references/ford-galaxy-mk2/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the pre-facelift exterior represents the full
# generation. The lamp internals, wheel spokes, bumper contours and door seams
# are simplified; registration characters, badge lettering and the seat
# interior are omitted. The mirror span is estimated at 2.180 m.


